Subject: [PATCH] apps: register the statically-linked pkcs11-provider at CLI startup

openssl.wasm links pkcs11-provider and a PKCS#11 engine statically, and
registers the provider with OSSL_PROVIDER_add_builtin() from
pqctoday_cms_init() (wasm/openssl-studio/shims/cms_provider_init.c). That registration
is per-runtime, and openssl.wasm is built with -sEXIT_RUNTIME=1, so EVERY
callMain() starts a fresh runtime with nothing registered.

Without this hook, a CLI command touching a `pkcs11:` URI only works if
the embedding JS called _pqctoday_cms_init() on that exact module instance
first. Calling it from apps_startup() makes the provider available to
every command in every instance -- which the CMS/S-MIME workshop, the TLS
simulator's HSM mode, and OpenSSL Studio all depend on. Known in the JS as
"Fix A" (see the comment block in cms.worker.ts).

Recovered 2026-07-24: this patch previously existed only inside a
gitignored openssl-3.6.2-src tree on one machine. When that tree went
missing, a rebuild from pristine source silently produced a binary where
pkcs11: URIs no longer resolved in any CLI command.

--- a/apps/openssl.c
+++ b/apps/openssl.c
@@ -74,6 +74,21 @@
     (void)setup_engine_loader();
 
     /*
+     * pqctoday "Fix A": register the statically-linked pkcs11-provider in
+     * this runtime's global lib ctx. openssl.wasm is built -sEXIT_RUNTIME=1,
+     * so every callMain() starts a fresh runtime and the registration made by
+     * a previous command is gone; without this, `pkcs11:` URIs only work if
+     * the embedding JS called _pqctoday_cms_init() on that exact module
+     * instance first. Idempotent (returns 1 when already loaded). The return
+     * code is ignored on purpose: a build or run with no usable PKCS#11
+     * module must still run every non-pkcs11 command normally.
+     */
+    {
+        extern int pqctoday_cms_init(void);
+        (void)pqctoday_cms_init();
+    }
+
+    /*
      * NOTE: This is an undocumented feature required for testing only.
      * There are no guarantees that it will exist in future builds.
      */
